            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0276" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg180"/>

                <head>No. 124.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Washburne.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 9,
                        1871</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 335.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The following extract from a report made by
                    Minister Leon to the Congress of Ecuador, a copy of which accompanied a dispatch
                    of the 21st of August last, from our minister at Quito, is transmitted for your
                    information: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Our citizens in Paris having been exposed to the consequences of the
                            horrible Franco-German war without any Ecuadorian diplomatic agent which
                            could protect their persons and property, found in the minister
                            plenipotentiary (the Hon. E. B. Washburne) of the United States of
                            America aid and protection.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
